# No bot Co-authored-by in commits

This repository runs `check-bot-coauthors` (post-no-bills) on every PR. Commit messages must not include `Co-authored-by` trailers or bot identities (for example `cursoragent@cursor.com`). Put model attribution in the PR body using the required `Generated with <model> for <job> in <tool> via <host>.` line (see `.github/CONTRIBUTING.md`), not in commit trailers.

After every `git commit` in this repo:

1. Run `git log -1 --format=%B` and check for a `Co-authored-by` line.
2. If one is present and the commit is still unpushed and was created in this session, amend the message to remove only that trailer, then push.
3. If the bad trailer is already on the remote, tell the user and rewrite with `git push --force-with-lease` only when they have asked to fix that commit.
